From da5862cd3dc77545eae19fa7a71a5aae0cb4f751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:08:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(gate): split the keep_law and level_links tests into
 cases

Each slow test of keep_law and level_links was one loop over its
cases. Each case is now its own test, in a module with the old test
name, so libtest runs the cases in parallel. No assert or expected
value changed.

- keep_law: 8 -> 31 tests (keep_law.rs 14, keep_law/stock_source.rs
  13, keep_law/mcp.rs 4). Binary 82.0 s -> 68.0 s in debug.
- level_links: 7 -> 25 tests (level_links.rs 22,
  level_links/choices.rs 3). Binary 73.2 s -> 36.6 s in debug.

whole_model_pocket runs in 2.1 s since #1716 and is not changed.
lathe_field_sim is not changed: its slowest test is one field-engine
job of about 107 s, and a split gives no gain.

Refs #1715

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
